From: Sebastian Huang <sebastian_huang@accton.com>
Subject: [PATCH] backports: do not redefine timer_container_of

Out-of-tree modules built against the backport headers, such as
batman-adv, may already provide timer_container_of() for kernels older
than 6.16 in their own compat header. Only define it when it is not
defined yet, so they build with -Werror.

--- a/backport-include/linux/timer.h
+++ b/backport-include/linux/timer.h
@@ -60,7 +60,7 @@
 	container_of(callback_timer, typeof(*var), timer_fieldname)
 #endif
 
-#if LINUX_VERSION_IS_LESS(6,16,0)
+#if LINUX_VERSION_IS_LESS(6,16,0) && !defined(timer_container_of)
 #define timer_container_of(var, callback_timer, timer_fieldname)	\
 	container_of(callback_timer, typeof(*var), timer_fieldname)
 #endif
